 {
  "unit": "item:rl",
  "verdict": "fail",
  "reason": "meat -> flesh at L1: 'flesh' is broader than meat (meat is animal flesh eaten as food; flesh is also human body tissue and fruit pulp), so this is a broader-word match, not same meaning. An 8-year-old reads 'flesh' as skin/body, and the gloss shown ('soft tissue of the body of a vertebrate: mainly muscle tissue and fat') describes body tissue, not food."
 },
