  "reason": "aqua -> cyan are near colour shades, not synonyms. Aqua is a blue-green (aquamarine/turquoise family) and cyan is the printing primary; they coincide only in web colour codes. Aqua's main sense is also 'water'. This is a related-word match, too loose for 'Same meaning'."
